{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And every daughter who inherits a portion.</b> That she had no brother, after the land was apportioned; therefore Scripture said a second time, ״ולא תסוב נחלה״ — 'and the inheritance shall not turn.' For this reason the custom in Israel regarding a daughter who inherits a portion, when she transgresses this and wishes to marry into another tribe, was that they would call her זונה — a zonah — and she would forfeit the inheritance of her father's house. This is what is written (Judges 11:1): ״ויפתח הגלעדי היה גבור חיל והוא בן אשה זונה״ — 'Now Jephthah the Gileadite was a mighty warrior, and he was the son of a zonah.' For the mother of Jephthah was a daughter who inherited a portion, and she married into another tribe; for the intent is not a zonah in the literal sense, heaven forbid, and so Jonathan rendered it (in the Targum). And it is possible to say that ״ולא תסוב נחלה״ speaks of the souls, and therefore it mentioned a second time ״ולא תסוב נחלה״, and likewise the word ״ידבקו״ — 'they shall cling' — for the first is clinging of body and the second is clinging of souls."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 36, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:38:05.010055277Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}